<v Sheldon Goldstein>My hearing is not that great.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我的听力不太好。

00:35:06.110 --> 00:35:06.740
<v Jonathan Goldstein>OK.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>OK。

00:35:06.740 --> 00:35:14.330
<v Sheldon Goldstein>And when I heard the first message I'm saying, who the heck is that? I don't know anybody by that name.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>当我听到第一条留言时，我说，那个人到底是谁？我不认识那个名字的人。

00:35:14.330 --> 00:35:37.220
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Sheldon now lives outside of Fort Lauderdale, but my few memories of him are from when he lived in upstate New York. I remember he lived in a trailer. I remember that he worked at a local prison, that he smoked cigars, that he looked a little like my father, but was hunched like the world was weighing down on him. And he always wore this expression on his face that seemed to say, you got to be kidding me.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>谢尔顿现在住在劳德代尔堡郊外，但我对他为数不多的记忆来自于他住在美国北部的时候。我记得他住在一个拖车里。我记得他在当地监狱工作，他抽雪茄，他看起来有点像我父亲，但驼着背，好像世界都在压迫着他。他总是带着那种似乎在说“你在开玩笑吧”的表情。

00:35:37.220 --> 00:35:39.800
<v Jonathan Goldstein>You're keeping OK? You're keeping occupied?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>你还好吗？你有事情做吗？

00:35:39.800 --> 00:35:50.060
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Yeah. I read a lot. I go to the gym. I go shopping, you know, here and there, little things here and there.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>嗯。我读很多书。我去健身房。我去购物，你知道，这儿那儿的，零碎的小事。

00:35:50.060 --> 00:35:53.120
<v Jonathan Goldstein>And so you still go-- how often do you go to the gym?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>那你还是会——你多久去一次健身房？

00:35:53.120 --> 00:35:55.700
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Three times a week.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>一周三次。

00:35:55.700 --> 00:36:08.800
<v Jonathan Goldstein>My father also goes to the gym. That's a part of his routine also. He was happy to hear from you on his 80th birthday.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>我父亲也去健身房。这也是他习惯的一部分。他在他80岁生日时很高兴接到你的电话。

00:36:08.800 --> 00:36:14.700
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Yeah. Well, he didn't call me on my 85th though.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>嗯。好吧，他在我85岁生日时没打电话给我。

00:36:14.700 --> 00:36:24.220
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Tit, meet tat.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>礼尚往来，见面谈吧。

00:36:24.220 --> 00:36:32.430
<v Sheldon Goldstein>To be honest with you, I've been-- in the last few years, I've been a loner.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>老实跟你说，我一直是——在过去几年里，我一直是个独行侠。

