<v Jonathan Goldstein>This is the point of the story for my father. It proves once and for all how his mother loved Sheldon more than she loved him. Sheldon didn't move out with her. And after a year, their mother returned. And together Buzz and Sheldon grew up under the same roof, in the same bedroom, often sleeping under the same blanket, each knowing who the mother had chosen, and each having to do their best to carry on and live life with the burden of that knowledge.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>这就是我父亲讲述故事的重点。它一劳永逸地证明了母亲爱谢尔顿胜过爱他。谢尔顿没跟她搬走。一年后，他们的母亲回来了。巴兹和谢尔顿一起在同一个屋檐下、同一个卧室里长大，经常睡在同一条毯子下，每个人都知道母亲选择了谁，每个人都必须尽力背负着这种知识的负担继续生活下去。

