00:47:09.170 --> 00:47:11.440
<v Buzz Goldstein>Oh. It spread.
<v Buzz Goldstein>哦。扩散了。

00:47:11.440 --> 00:47:26.050
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I said, it's in her liver? I said, what?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我说，在她的肝脏里？我说，什么？

00:47:26.050 --> 00:47:36.750
<v Sheldon Goldstein>You know where I usually eat when I come in by myself? By the bar. They've got a waitress there who always waits on me. She takes good care of me.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你知道我通常一个人进来时在哪里吃饭吗？在酒吧。那里有个女招待总是招待我。她很照顾我。

00:47:36.750 --> 00:47:45.420
<v Jonathan Goldstein>For dinner, Sheldon takes us to a local Outback Steakhouse. As people walk by, he provides a running commentary of an elderly couple--
<v Jonathan Goldstein>晚餐时，谢尔顿带我们去了一家当地的Outback牛排馆。当人们走过时，他提供了对一对老年夫妇的实况解说——

00:47:45.420 --> 00:47:50.310
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Don't get like that couple, whatever you do. It's time for the execution.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>不管怎么样，别变得像那对夫妇那样。死刑时间到了。

00:47:50.310 --> 00:47:52.010
<v Jonathan Goldstein>--of an overweight couple.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>——对一对超重夫妇。

00:47:52.010 --> 00:47:57.460
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Boy, are they fat. People are fat today.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>天哪，他们真胖。今天的人真胖。

00:47:57.460 --> 00:48:04.210
<v Jonathan Goldstein>It's as though he's sharpening his wit, readying it for the main event, teasing my dad about Canada.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>就好像他在磨练自己的智慧，为重头戏做准备，打趣我爸爸关于加拿大的事。

00:48:04.210 --> 00:48:07.100
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I don't know how you could take Canada all year round.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我不明白你怎么能整年忍受加拿大。

00:48:07.100 --> 00:48:13.600
<v Buzz Goldstein>Why? We've got nice neighbors. It's nice. It's OK. What was I going to say?
<v Buzz Goldstein>为什么？我们有好邻居。很好。还行。我刚想说什么来着？

00:48:13.600 --> 00:48:16.600
<v Sheldon Goldstein>You're living in the same place for how many years?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你在同一个地方住了多少年了？

00:48:16.600 --> 00:48:23.440
<v Buzz Goldstein>Oh, about-- over 35, 38 years, something like that. I'm happy there. Yeah, yeah.
<v Buzz Goldstein>哦，大概——超过35、38年之类的吧。我住在那里很开心。是的，是的。

00:48:23.440 --> 00:48:54.310
<v Jonathan Goldstein>For my father, I know this is a touchy subject, believing, as he always has, that Sheldon looks down on him for the dinkiness of his Canadian life and home. It's like a constant reminder of just who is second best. Later, my father will repeat Sheldon's words. You're still living in that same place, he'll say, for how many years? But just then, I watched my father clench and unclench his jaw, as he does when he is brooding. I know he's trying to take the high road, trying not to ruin the evening.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>对我父亲来说，我知道这是一个敏感话题，他一直认为谢尔顿因为他平庸的加拿大生活和住所而看不起他。这就像时刻提醒他谁才是第二名。后来，我父亲会重复谢尔顿的话。“你还在住那个地方，”他会说，“多少年了？”但就在那时，我看着父亲紧咬着牙关，就像他心事重重时那样。我知道他在试图保持高姿态，尽量不破坏气氛。

00:48:54.310 --> 00:48:59.210
<v Sheldon Goldstein>What, $200.30? Are they kidding?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>什么，200.30美元？开玩笑吗？

00:48:59.210 --> 00:49:05.130
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Sheldon invites us back to his place for cookies, but my father says he isn't up for it.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>谢尔顿邀请我们去他家吃饼干，但我父亲说他没那个精神。

00:49:05.130 --> 00:49:06.160
<v Buzz Goldstein>Thank you. Good night.
<v Buzz Goldstein>谢谢。晚安。

00:49:06.160 --> 00:49:15.330
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Yep.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>没错。

00:49:15.330 --> 00:50:01.500
<v Jonathan Goldstein>As we walk through the restaurant parking lot to the car, my father is silent. I find myself feeling protective of him, like maybe encouraging this trip had been a bad idea, only making things worse. After midnight, lying awake in our hotel-- my father insisted we stay at one-- I lay in bed thinking about that day in 1939 when my grandmother came back for Sheldon, not my father. For my father, not only did it push him away from Sheldon, making him feel jealous and resentful, but it also cast a shadow over the rest of his life, causing him to always feel passed over. He's mellowed with age, but as a kid I saw it come out in all kinds of ways-- always sensitive to slights, ready for a fight at the smallest perceived offense.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>当我们走过餐馆停车场去车边时，父亲沉默了。我发现自己开始保护他，觉得鼓励这次旅行可能是一个糟糕的主意，只会让事情变得更糟。半夜，躺在旅馆里——父亲坚持我们住在那里——我躺在床上想着1939年的那一天，祖母回来接谢尔顿而不是父亲。对我父亲来说，这不仅把他推离了谢尔顿，让他感到嫉妒和怨恨，还在他余生的心头投下了阴影，使他总是觉得自己被忽视。他随年龄增长变得圆滑了一些，但小时候我看到它以各种方式表现出来——总是对冷落敏感，准备为最小的冒犯而争吵。

00:50:01.500 --> 00:50:23.030
<v Jonathan Goldstein>I wonder if there's a different way for my father to see things. If there is, the only living person in this world who can help is Sheldon. When their mom left, Sheldon was nine, my father five. Sheldon would have understood a lot more than my father.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>我想知道是否有另一种方式能让父亲看待事物。如果有，世界上唯一能帮忙的人就是谢尔顿。母亲离开时，谢尔顿9岁，我父亲5岁。谢尔顿理解的东西比父亲多得多。

00:50:23.030 --> 00:50:45.370
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Yesterday, Buzz and Sheldon talked like a couple of kids who used to play stickball in the old neighborhood. Today, if me and my big fat meddling yap have any sway, they'll have a chance to talk as men, as brothers even. Because if not now, when? Day two.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>昨天，巴兹和谢尔顿像两个在旧街区玩拍球的孩子一样交谈。今天，如果我和我那张爱管闲事的大嘴巴有任何影响力，他们将有机会作为男人，甚至作为兄弟谈谈。因为如果不是现在，那是何时？第二天。

00:50:45.370 --> 00:50:46.900
<v Buzz Goldstein>This is a damn good cigar.
<v Buzz Goldstein>这雪茄真不错。

00:50:46.900 --> 00:50:48.010
<v Sheldon Goldstein>He sent me--
<v Sheldon Goldstein>他送我——

00:50:48.010 --> 00:50:51.700
<v Buzz Goldstein>Oh, Dominican Republic. They make a damn good cigar in Dominican Republic. What are you talking about?
<v Buzz Goldstein>哦，多米尼加共和国。他们在多米尼加共和国做的雪茄真不错。你在说什么呢？

00:50:51.700 --> 00:51:03.230
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Despite the difficulties of last night, the coin is flipped back to the good side. Sheldon offers my father a cigar and with the cigar some cigar talk, some pretty foul cigar talk.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>尽管昨晚有困难，但硬币又翻回了好的一面。谢尔顿给了父亲一支雪茄，还谈论了一些雪茄话题，一些非常粗俗的雪茄话题。

00:51:03.230 --> 00:51:12.150
<v Sheldon Goldstein>We're riding on Queens Boulevard. Johnny's in the back seat with The Who. He's got his naked ass up in the air. And he's humping--
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我们在皇后大道上骑行。乔尼在后座和The Who在一起。他光着屁股在空中。他在做活塞运动——

00:51:12.150 --> 00:51:12.940
<v Buzz Goldstein>[LAUGHS]
<v Buzz Goldstein>[笑声]

00:51:12.940 --> 00:51:23.020
<v Sheldon Goldstein>The funny thing is we had to stop for a light. And there's a truck driver sitting in the cab up high. God, that was funny.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>有趣的是我们必须在红绿灯处停下。有个卡车司机坐在高高的驾驶室里。天哪，那太好笑了。

00:51:23.020 --> 00:51:28.090
<v Buzz Goldstein>[LAUGHS]
<v Buzz Goldstein>[笑声]

00:51:28.090 --> 00:51:29.870
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Have you guys missed each other?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>你们想念彼此吗？

00:51:29.870 --> 00:51:30.200
<v Sheldon Goldstein>What?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>什么？

00:51:30.200 --> 00:51:32.670
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Do you miss each other?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>你们想念彼此吗？

00:51:32.670 --> 00:51:39.100
<v Sheldon Goldstein>You know, he asks the weirdest questions. What is he, a broad?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你知道，他总是问些最奇怪的问题。他是娘们儿吗？

00:51:39.100 --> 00:51:41.600
<v Jonathan Goldstein>No. I mean-- I don't know.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>不。我是说——我不知道。

00:51:41.600 --> 00:51:53.420
<v Ira Glass>Eager to prove to my Uncle Sheldon that in spite of the fact I'm wearing my wife's travel deodorant, I am indeed not a broad. I allow them to return to more pressing matters, their prostates.
<v Ira Glass>急于向谢尔顿叔叔证明，尽管我穿着妻子的旅行除臭剂，但我确实不是娘们儿。我让他们回归到更紧迫的问题上，他们的前列腺。

00:51:53.420 --> 00:52:04.750
<v Sheldon Goldstein>The guy says, Jesus. He says, your prostate feels like the moon craters in there. I said thank you, Doctor. Thought he was complimenting me.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>那家伙说，天哪。他说，你的前列腺摸起来像里面的月球陨石坑。我说谢谢，医生。以为他在赞美我。

00:52:04.750 --> 00:52:12.140
<v Jonathan Goldstein>So if I could steer this away from the prostates-- so my father said that it's significant to him to have come. What do you say?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>如果我能把话题从前列腺上引开——我父亲说这次来对他很重要。你觉得呢？

00:52:12.140 --> 00:52:14.270
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I agree with whatever he said.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>他说的什么我同意什么。

00:52:14.270 --> 00:52:15.370
<v Jonathan Goldstein>But what about you?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>那你是怎么想的？

00:52:15.370 --> 00:52:19.530
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I said I agree with whatever he said. Do you want a written contract?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我说他说的什么我同意什么。你想要一份书面合同吗？

00:52:19.530 --> 00:52:22.310
<v Jonathan Goldstein>No, no. I'm happy with that.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>不，不。我对此很高兴。

00:52:22.310 --> 00:52:29.260
<v Ira Glass>It feels like I'm getting a taste of what growing up with Sheldon might have been like. So again, I make my move.
<v Ira Glass>感觉我像是在品尝和谢尔顿一起长大的感觉。所以我再次行动。

00:52:29.260 --> 00:52:51.680
<v Jonathan Goldstein>So I have some questions just about-- because of the stories that I know from my father, but I'm curious what your take is because you were older. Do you remember what was going on when your mom-- when your mother left originally, like why and what was going on?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>我有几个问题想问，因为我从父亲那里知道这些故事，但我好奇你的看法，因为你年纪大。你还记得你妈妈当初离开时发生了什么吗，为什么以及当时发生了什么？

00:52:51.680 --> 00:52:55.630
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Didn't you cover this ground before yesterday?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>昨天不是谈过这些了吗？

00:52:55.630 --> 00:53:03.480
<v Jonathan Goldstein>But from my father's perspective, the way I understood it was always you were the favorite. Did you feel that way?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>但从我父亲的角度来看，我的理解一直是你最受宠。你有这种感觉吗？

00:53:03.480 --> 00:53:06.780
<v Ira Glass>At this point, Sheldon's face suddenly softens.
<v Ira Glass>此时，谢尔顿的脸突然柔和下来。

00:53:06.780 --> 00:53:10.270
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I always felt that I got the short end of the stick.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我一直觉得我处境最糟。

00:53:10.270 --> 00:53:15.490
<v Buzz Goldstein>Yeah, but you were kind of a favorite with my mom.
<v Buzz Goldstein>是，但你确实挺受我妈喜欢的。

00:53:15.490 --> 00:53:30.630
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Yeah, maybe with Mom 'cause maybe temperamentally we were closer than I was with my father. My father never gave me spit. Did you ever get any money from my father?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>是，可能和妈在一起是因为性格上我们可能比我和父亲更近。父亲从来没给过我什么。你从父亲那里拿到过钱吗？

00:53:30.630 --> 00:53:31.860
<v Buzz Goldstein>Can't remember.
<v Buzz Goldstein>记不得了。

00:53:31.860 --> 00:53:33.870
<v Sheldon Goldstein>You never got a dime.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你从来没拿到过一毛钱。

00:53:33.870 --> 00:53:35.470
<v Buzz Goldstein>No, can't remember.
<v Buzz Goldstein>不，记不得了。

00:53:35.470 --> 00:53:38.650
<v Sheldon Goldstein>You never-- one time I sprained my ankle so bad.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你从来——有一次我脚踝扭得特别厉害。

00:53:38.650 --> 00:53:41.070
<v Buzz Goldstein>Oh, I'll never forget that. That was terrible.
<v Buzz Goldstein>哦，我永远不会忘记那个。那太可怕了。

00:53:41.070 --> 00:53:46.900
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I laid in that bed. And he says to me, you lazy bum.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我躺在床上。他跟我说，你个懒流浪汉。

00:53:46.900 --> 00:53:48.430
<v Buzz Goldstein>Yeah.
<v Buzz Goldstein>是啊。

00:53:48.430 --> 00:53:52.100
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Man, he went off on me that time. Whoo.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>天哪，那次他对我发了火。哇。

00:53:52.100 --> 00:53:57.650
<v Buzz Goldstein>He took Sheldon once. Sheldon happened to say the word [BLEEP].
<v Buzz Goldstein>他带谢尔顿去过一次。谢尔顿碰巧说了个[脏话]词。

00:53:57.650 --> 00:54:02.760
<v Sheldon Goldstein>He came in with that [BLEEP] strap swinging with the buckle.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>他带着那个[脏话]带着扣子的带子挥舞着进来了。

00:54:02.760 --> 00:54:08.970
<v Buzz Goldstein>And I can understand it leaving a feeling of resentment and dislike.
<v Buzz Goldstein>我可以理解那会留下一种怨恨和厌恶的感觉。

00:54:08.970 --> 00:54:16.800
<v Sheldon Goldstein>That was his way of communicating with us-- smack, smack, and then--
<v Sheldon Goldstein>那是他与我们交流的方式——啪啪，然后——

00:54:16.800 --> 00:54:18.510
<v Buzz Goldstein>What a way. Yeah.
<v Buzz Goldstein>真是个好方法。是啊。

00:54:18.510 --> 00:54:22.250
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Was he easier on you, do you think?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>你认为他对你更宽容吗？

00:54:22.250 --> 00:54:25.000
<v Buzz Goldstein>He wasn't that easy, but he was tough on Sheldon.
<v Buzz Goldstein>他没那么宽容，但他对谢尔顿很严厉。

00:54:25.000 --> 00:54:27.720
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I know you were closer to him than I was.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我知道你比我更接近他。

00:54:27.720 --> 00:54:29.110
<v Buzz Goldstein>Yeah.
<v Buzz Goldstein>是的。

00:54:29.110 --> 00:54:33.930
<v Sheldon Goldstein>A lot of things that went on and you didn't understand really what was going on.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>发生了很多事情，而你并没有真正理解发生了什么。

00:54:33.930 --> 00:54:36.760
<v Buzz Goldstein>No, I didn't. So you had a different take?
<v Buzz Goldstein>不，我没懂。所以你有不同的看法？

00:54:36.760 --> 00:54:38.780
<v Jonathan Goldstein>Why? Are you surprised by--
<v Jonathan Goldstein>怎么？你对——感到惊讶吗？

00:54:38.780 --> 00:54:40.510
<v Buzz Goldstein>But I was a kid. I didn't understand it.
<v Buzz Goldstein>但我当时是个孩子。我不明白。

00:54:40.510 --> 00:54:44.380
<v Jonathan Goldstein>But you didn't know that Sheldon was getting it so bad?
<v Jonathan Goldstein>但你不知道谢尔顿受了这么多苦？

00:54:44.380 --> 00:54:46.510
<v Buzz Goldstein>No.
<v Buzz Goldstein>不。

00:54:46.510 --> 00:55:19.020
<v Jonathan Goldstein>In Buzz's telling, their father was always a more or less benign, childish figure incapable of expressing his feelings and so given to temper tantrums. For Buzz, it was their mother who was the manipulator, the woman who played the brothers off each other. But hearing Sheldon's take, it sounds like maybe their mother didn't come to take Sheldon because she loved him best, but simply because he needed more protecting from their father.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>在巴兹的叙述中，他们的父亲一直是个或多或少良性、幼稚的人物，无法表达自己的情感，因此容易发脾气。对巴兹来说，是母亲才是操纵者，是那个让兄弟反目的女人。但听了谢尔顿的说法，听起来母亲当初不来接谢尔顿并不是因为最爱他，而仅仅是因为他需要更多来自父亲的保护。

00:55:19.020 --> 00:55:34.920
<v Jonathan Goldstein>For the first time during our trip, I can see my father considering Sheldon's point of view, actually taking it in. I know it's intense for him because he can't even meet Sheldon's eyes. Instead, he looks at me, addresses his comments to me.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>这是我们旅行中第一次，我看到父亲在考虑谢尔顿的观点，真的听进去了。我知道这对他来说很强烈，因为他甚至无法直视谢尔顿的眼睛。相反，他看着我，向我发表评论。

00:55:34.920 --> 00:55:48.320
<v Buzz Goldstein>It sad that my father had such a negative impact on him, just awful. Because he had so much going for him. He was a wonderful son. He worked hard. He was a good boy. He went to school.
<v Buzz Goldstein>悲哀的是，我父亲对他有如此负面的影响，太可怕了。因为他本来有很多优点。他是个好儿子。他工作努力。他是个好孩子。他上了学。

00:55:48.320 --> 00:55:50.470
<v Sheldon Goldstein>You're talking like I'm a failure in life.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你说的好像我是个失败者。

00:55:50.470 --> 00:55:52.710
<v Buzz Goldstein>No, you weren't a failure. That's the thing that I'm saying.
<v Buzz Goldstein>不，你不是失败者。这就是我说的重点。

00:55:52.710 --> 00:55:53.750
<v Sheldon Goldstein>No, I am.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>不，我是。

00:55:53.750 --> 00:55:58.470
<v Buzz Goldstein>You weren't a failure. But all I'm saying is that emotionally he left an impact on you.
<v Buzz Goldstein>你不是失败者。我只是说他在情感上对你留下了影响。

00:55:58.470 --> 00:56:11.400
<v Sheldon Goldstein>It took a long time for me to get out of that emotion. And now I'm at peace with myself. I can talk about him and laugh about it.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我花了好长时间才从那种情绪中走出来。现在我对自己感到平静。我可以谈论他并以此为乐。

00:56:11.400 --> 00:56:12.810
<v Buzz Goldstein>Yeah, yeah.
<v Buzz Goldstein>是啊，是啊。

00:56:12.810 --> 00:56:20.260
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Now I want peace, quiet. I'm happy living by myself.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>现在我想要和平，安静。我一个人住很开心。

00:56:20.260 --> 00:56:22.390
<v Buzz Goldstein>Are you lonely, Sheldon?
<v Buzz Goldstein>谢尔顿，你寂寞吗？

00:56:22.390 --> 00:56:23.350
<v Sheldon Goldstein>No.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>不。

00:56:23.350 --> 00:56:28.640
<v Buzz Goldstein>No?
<v Buzz Goldstein>不？

00:56:28.640 --> 00:56:57.630
<v Jonathan Goldstein>The last time my father saw my grandfather in full health, my dad was visiting from Canada. My grandfather asked my father to drive him to the cemetery to visit his parents' grave. And once there, my grandfather wept inconsolably. Later that day, he would succumb to a stroke and shortly after be moved to a nursing home. With Sheldon being more local, the burden of my grandfather's care fell mainly to Sheldon. It seems like a lot of the family's burdens fell to Sheldon.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>父亲最后一次见到祖父完全健康时，父亲正在从加拿大来探访。祖父请父亲开车带他去墓地探望他父母的墓。到了那里，祖父伤心地哭了起来。那天晚些时候，他中风了，不久后被送进疗养院。由于谢尔顿住得近，照顾祖父的重担主要落在了谢尔顿身上。似乎家庭的很多负担都落在了谢尔顿肩上。

00:56:57.630 --> 00:57:06.450
<v Buzz Goldstein>They put a lot of the responsibility on him that my dad should have been taking that responsibility. And he shouldered that.
<v Buzz Goldstein>他们把很多责任都推给他，而原本我爸应该承担这些责任。他承担下来了。

00:57:06.450 --> 00:57:17.460
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Who was going to take care of you? Who was going to take you to school? [INAUDIBLE] I remember one time I was late or something. You stood outside that screen door, crying.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>谁来照顾你？谁来送你上学？[听不清]我记得有一次我迟到了什么的。你站在纱门外面哭。

00:57:17.460 --> 00:57:18.570
<v Buzz Goldstein>Yeah, yeah.
<v Buzz Goldstein>是啊，是啊。

00:57:18.570 --> 00:57:21.400
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I'd say, Buzzy, I'm here. I'm here.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我会说，巴兹，我在这。我在这。

00:57:21.400 --> 00:57:24.240
<v Buzz Goldstein>He was good to me. A lot of times he was good to me.
<v Buzz Goldstein>他对我很好。很多时候他对我很好。

00:57:24.240 --> 00:57:24.900
<v Sheldon Goldstein>A lot of times I was mean to you.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>很多时候我对你很刻薄。

00:57:24.900 --> 00:57:35.180
<v Buzz Goldstein>Mean, you know-- you were my older brother. You used to knock the [BLEEP] out of me sometimes, but that's the way it is with brothers. Yeah.
<v Buzz Goldstein>刻薄，你知道——你是哥哥。有时候你确实把我[脏话]揍了一顿，但兄弟之间就是这样。是的。

00:57:35.180 --> 00:57:37.800
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I was good in some ways. Some ways I was mean.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>在某些方面我很好。在某些方面我很刻薄。

00:57:37.800 --> 00:57:42.000
<v Buzz Goldstein>Well, who is not? Who is not? Who is not?
<v Buzz Goldstein>嗯，谁不是呢？谁不是呢？谁不是呢？

00:57:42.000 --> 00:57:57.240
<v Jonathan Goldstein>So if you feel like you were compelled to see each other now because you knew that it's a now or never kind of thing, then it means that it was important to you both, right, to see each other.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>所以如果你觉得你们现在必须见到对方，因为你们知道这是最后的机会，那意味着你们两个都认为见到对方很重要，对吧？

00:57:57.240 --> 00:57:58.320
<v Sheldon Goldstein>You want to take that?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你要回答吗？

00:57:58.320 --> 00:57:58.500
<v Buzz Goldstein>Sure.
<v Buzz Goldstein>当然。

00:57:58.500 --> 00:57:59.070
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I'm not. Go ahead.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我不想。你说吧。

00:57:59.070 --> 00:58:10.250
<v Buzz Goldstein>Yes. It's an easy answer-- yes. Yes, because we're not getting any younger. What's down the road? I'm 80. He's 85.
<v Buzz Goldstein>是的。答案很简单——是的。是的，因为我们都在变老。未来会怎样？我80岁了。他85岁了。

00:58:10.250 --> 00:58:25.010
<v Buzz Goldstein>I mean, because there was a lot of water under the bridge, and we want to close that bridge now. I want to feel easy now. I want to say now he's going to be 86, I want to call him on his birthday and say happy birthday to him now. I'm not going to stand any [BLEEP] ceremonies anymore.
<v Buzz Goldstein>我是说，因为覆水难收，我们现在想结束那道桥了。我想现在感到轻松。我想现在他要86岁了，我打电话给他说生日快乐。我再也不想搞什么[脏话]仪式了。

00:58:25.010 --> 00:58:38.750
<v Jonathan Goldstein>As my father speaks, as per his brother's example, dropping F bombs like he's in a Guy Ritchie film, Sheldon keeps his arms crossed and his eyes shut tight. He's quiet for several seconds, and then he reaches out to pet his cat.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>随着父亲说话，正如他弟弟的榜样一样，像在盖·里奇的电影里那样骂着粗口，谢尔顿双臂交叉，双眼紧闭。他安静了几秒钟，然后伸手去抚摸他的猫。

00:58:38.750 --> 00:58:42.440
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Should I leave you the cat in my will if anything happens?
<v Sheldon Goldstein>如果发生什么事，我该把猫留给你吗？

00:58:42.440 --> 00:58:45.890
<v Buzz Goldstein>If anything happens, I'll take care of the cat. I'll take care of the cat.
<v Buzz Goldstein>如果发生什么事，我会照顾这只猫。我会照顾这只猫的。

00:58:45.890 --> 00:58:47.590
<v Sheldon Goldstein>[LAUGHS]
<v Sheldon Goldstein>[笑声]

00:58:47.590 --> 00:58:49.970
<v Buzz Goldstein>I'm happy I came to see you. That I am.
<v Buzz Goldstein>我很高兴来见你。真的。

00:58:49.970 --> 00:59:02.310
<v Sheldon Goldstein>I'm happy you came here. That's good, very good. If either of you want to buy a house, that one is for sale over there.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>我很高兴你来这里。那很好，非常好。如果你们谁想买房子，那边那栋正在出售。

00:59:02.310 --> 00:59:26.970
<v Jonathan Goldstein>When it's time to leave, Sheldon walks us outside. But before we get into the rental, he points across the lawn to his neighbor's house. He tells my father that it's for sale, and then he tells him the asking price. And my father says that doesn't sound bad at all. And Sheldon says that, what, with Canada being so bloody cold, my father should consider moving to Florida. And my father says maybe he will.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>是时候离开时，谢尔顿送我们出去。但在我们坐进租的车之前，他指向草坪对面邻居的房子。他告诉我父亲房子正在出售，然后报出了要价。我父亲说听起来还不错。谢尔顿说，加拿大天气这么冷，父亲应该考虑搬到佛罗里达。我父亲说也许他会。

00:59:26.970 --> 00:59:27.940
<v Buzz Goldstein>All right. You take care.
<v Buzz Goldstein>好吧。保重。

00:59:27.940 --> 00:59:29.210
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Water under the bridge.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>覆水难收。

00:59:29.210 --> 00:59:29.520
<v Buzz Goldstein>Take care.
<v Buzz Goldstein>保重。

00:59:29.520 --> 00:59:33.100
<v Sheldon Goldstein>Take care, you too. Safe trip, both of yous.
<v Sheldon Goldstein>你也保重。旅途平安，你们两个。

00:59:33.100 --> 00:59:36.930
<v Buzz Goldstein>Thank you, thank you. We'll speak. We'll speak.
<v Buzz Goldstein>谢谢，谢谢。我们会保持联系。会保持联系的。

00:59:36.930 --> 00:59:48.520
<v Jonathan Goldstein>They don't get too emotional. They don't even hug goodbye. They just shake hands. And with that, it feels like Buzz has forgiven Sheldon and Sheldon has forgiven Buzz.
<v Jonathan Goldstein>他们没有表现得太情绪化。他们甚至没有拥抱告别。他们只是握了握手。这样，感觉巴兹原谅了谢尔顿，谢尔顿也原谅了巴兹。

00:59:48.520 --> 00:59:50.740
<v Gps>Turn right on Northwest Bedford Drive.
<v Gps>在西北贝德福德大道右转。

00:59:50.740 --> 01:00:16.760
<v Buzz Goldstein>Oh my god. I feel so different now, you know that? I feel different, Johnny. I just feel so different. This has taken a lot off my shoulders, you know?
<v Buzz Goldstein>天哪。我现在感觉太不一样了，你知道吗？我感觉不一样，乔尼。我感觉太不一样了。这让我肩上的担子减轻了很多，你知道吗？

